<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Industrial Machine Fault Monitoring (STM32) | Rajeswari T</title>
<meta name="description" content="Real-time machine fault monitoring using STM32 ADC with sound and temperature sensors.">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#020604">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="../assets/logo.svg">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="nebula"></div>
<canvas id="cosmos"></canvas>
<div class="cursor-glow"></div>
<header class="nav">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a href="../index.html" class="brand"><img src="../assets/logo.svg" alt="Rajeswari T logo"><span>RAJESWARI T<small>EMBEDDED // ECE</small></span></a>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="../index.html#about">About</a></li>
      <li><a href="../index.html#projects" class="active">Projects</a></li>
      <li><a href="../index.html#skills">Skills</a></li>
      <li><a href="../index.html#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
    <a href="../assets/Rajeswari_T_Resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="nav-cta">Resume ↗</a>
    <button class="menu-btn" aria-label="Menu"><span></span><span></span></button>
  </div>
</header>
<main>
<section class="p-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a href="../index.html#projects" class="back"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5M11 18l-6-6 6-6"/></svg> All projects</a>
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">P/04 · STM32 · ADC</div>
    <h1 class="reveal d1">Machine fault monitoring on <em>STM32.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead reveal d2">A real-time monitoring system that samples a machine's sound and temperature through the STM32's on-chip ADC and flags abnormal operation, a bare-metal foundation for industrial condition monitoring.</p>
    <div class="p-meta"><div class="panel reveal d0"><small>Type</small><b>Condition monitoring</b></div><div class="panel reveal d1"><small>Controller</small><b>STM32</b></div><div class="panel reveal d2"><small>Interface</small><b>On-chip ADC</b></div><div class="panel reveal d3"><small>IDE</small><b>STM32CubeIDE</b></div></div>
    <div class="panel p-diagram reveal"><svg viewBox="0 0 900 300" role="img" aria-label="System architecture diagram">
<defs>
<marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#3ee07a"/></marker>
<filter id="glow" x="-30%" y="-30%" width="160%" height="160%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="4" result="b"/><feMerge><feMergeNode in="b"/><feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic"/></feMerge></filter>
</defs><g><rect x="30" y="40" width="180" height="64" rx="10" fill="#08140d" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.45)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="120.0" y="66.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="500">Sound Sensor</text><text x="120.0" y="85.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#93a89b" style="fill:#93a89b">machine noise</text></g><g><rect x="30" y="196" width="180" height="64" rx="10" fill="#08140d" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.45)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="120.0" y="222.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="500">Temp Sensor</text><text x="120.0" y="241.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#93a89b" style="fill:#93a89b">surface heat</text></g><g><rect x="330" y="95" width="210" height="110" rx="10" fill="#0d2417" stroke="#3ee07a" stroke-width="1.4" filter="url(#glow)"/><text x="435.0" y="144.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="500">STM32</text><text x="435.0" y="163.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#93a89b" style="fill:#93a89b">ADC sampling + logic</text></g><g><rect x="680" y="60" width="190" height="64" rx="10" fill="#08140d" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.45)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="775.0" y="86.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="500">Normal</text><text x="775.0" y="105.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#93a89b" style="fill:#93a89b">within limits</text></g><g><rect x="680" y="176" width="190" height="64" rx="10" fill="#08140d" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.45)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="775.0" y="202.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="500">Fault Flag</text><text x="775.0" y="221.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#93a89b" style="fill:#93a89b">abnormal reading</text></g><path d="M210 72 C270 72 270 125 328 125" fill="none" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.25)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M210 72 C270 72 270 125 328 125" fill="none" stroke="#3ee07a" stroke-width="2" class="flow" marker-end="url(#arr)"/><text x="268" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" style="fill:#8cffb4">ADC CH</text><path d="M210 228 C270 228 270 175 328 175" fill="none" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.25)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M210 228 C270 228 270 175 328 175" fill="none" stroke="#3ee07a" stroke-width="2" class="flow" marker-end="url(#arr)"/><path d="M540 130 C610 130 610 92 678 92" fill="none" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.25)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M540 130 C610 130 610 92 678 92" fill="none" stroke="#3ee07a" stroke-width="2" class="flow" marker-end="url(#arr)"/><path d="M540 170 C610 170 610 208 678 208" fill="none" stroke="rgba(62,224,122,.25)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M540 170 C610 170 610 208 678 208" fill="none" stroke="#3ee07a" stroke-width="2" class="flow" marker-end="url(#arr)"/></svg><div class="cap">Fig. 1: Two analog sensors sampled by the STM32 ADC and classified as normal or fault.</div></div>
    <div class="p-body"><div class="panel p-block reveal"><h3>The goal</h3><p>Machines usually get noisier and hotter before they fail. This project captures both signals in real time on an industrial-grade microcontroller and turns them into a simple, immediate fault indication.</p></div><div class="panel p-block reveal"><h3>Why STM32</h3><p>STM32 is widely used in industrial embedded products. Working at the ADC level with STM32CubeIDE builds skills that transfer directly: peripheral configuration, sampling and real-time firmware.</p></div><div class="panel p-block reveal full"><h3>How it works</h3><div class="steps"><div class="step"><b>Configure</b><span>ADC channels and GPIO set up in STM32CubeIDE.</span></div><div class="step"><b>Sample</b><span>Sound and temperature sensors are read continuously through the ADC.</span></div><div class="step"><b>Evaluate</b><span>Firmware compares readings against expected operating ranges.</span></div><div class="step"><b>Indicate</b><span>Readings outside range raise a fault indication in real time.</span></div></div></div><div class="panel p-block reveal"><h3>Hardware</h3><table class="hw"><tr><td>STM32</td><td>ARM Cortex-M microcontroller</td></tr><tr><td>ADC</td><td>On-chip analog-to-digital converter for sensor input</td></tr><tr><td>Sound sensor</td><td>Captures machine noise level</td></tr><tr><td>Temperature sensor</td><td>Tracks machine heating</td></tr></table></div><div class="panel p-block reveal"><h3>What it builds toward</h3><ul><li><b>Foundation for SUMA-TEX:</b> the same sense-and-detect idea, later expanded to four modalities and ML.</li><li><b>Low-level control:</b> direct peripheral work instead of relying on high-level libraries.</li></ul></div></div>
    <div class="p-nav">
      <a class="panel" href="gas-shutdown.html"><small>← Previous</small><b>Gas Detection & Emergency Shutdown</b></a>
      <a class="panel" href="vector-aid.html"><small>Next →</small><b>Vector Aid: V2V Ambulance Alert</b></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
